WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:14.799
Unit ten: Social Media. Today you will give advice about social media with should and must.

4
00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:17.461
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.552
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:23.406
Platform.

7
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:27.693
Platform means a website or app where people share things.

8
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:30.294
TikTok is a popular platform.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.547
Your turn. Say: Platform.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.424
Platform.

11
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:38.964
Post.

12
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.542
Post means a message or photo you share online.

13
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.208
I liked her post about the festival.

14
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.515
Your turn. Say: Post.

15
00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.194
Post.

16
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:53.730
Follower.

17
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:57.320
Follower means a person who sees your posts.

18
00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:59.916
He has five hundred followers.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.728
Your turn. Say: Follower.

20
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.579
Follower.

21
00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:08.202
Comment.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:11.553
Comment means a written reply to a post.

23
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.033
Please write kind comments.

24
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.838
Your turn. Say: Comment.

25
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.504
Comment.

26
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:21.984
Viral.

27
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:25.726
Viral means shared very quickly by many people.

28
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:27.968
The funny video went viral.

29
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.992
Your turn. Say: Viral.

30
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:34.742
Viral.

31
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:36.519
Hashtag.

32
00:01:37.517 --> 00:01:41.316
Hashtag means a word with # that groups posts by topic.

33
00:01:41.917 --> 00:01:44.508
Use the hashtag #VisitCambodia.

34
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:47.699
Your turn. Say: Hashtag.

35
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:51.662
Hashtag.

36
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:53.627
Privacy setting.

37
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:57.789
Privacy setting means a control for who can see your things.

38
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.418
Check your privacy settings today.

39
00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:04.215
Your turn. Say: Privacy setting.

40
00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.312
Privacy setting.

41
00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.353
Digital footprint.

42
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:14.557
Digital footprint means everything about you that stays online.

43
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.196
Your digital footprint lasts forever.

44
00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:20.401
Your turn. Say: Digital footprint.

45
00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:24.581
Digital footprint.

46
00:02:25.317 --> 00:02:26.445
Influencer.

47
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.470
Influencer means a person online who affects what people do and buy.

48
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:34.350
The influencer reviews new phones.

49
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.835
Your turn. Say: Influencer.

50
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.829
Influencer.

51
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:43.677
Engagement.

52
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:48.018
Engagement means likes, comments and shares on a post.

53
00:02:48.617 --> 00:02:50.396
My post got high engagement.

54
00:02:50.983 --> 00:02:53.403
Your turn. Say: Engagement.

55
00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.256
Engagement.

56
00:02:58.017 --> 00:02:58.960
Algorithm.

57
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.971
Algorithm means the computer rules that choose what you see.

58
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.012
The algorithm shows me cooking videos.

59
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:09.304
Your turn. Say: Algorithm.

60
00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:13.156
Algorithm.

61
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:14.651
Trend.

62
00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.276
Trend means something popular for a short time.

63
00:03:18.883 --> 00:03:20.825
This dance is the latest trend.

64
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:23.616
Your turn. Say: Trend.

65
00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.282
Trend.

66
00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:31.834
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:34.880
Visal, do you use social media?

68
00:03:35.983 --> 00:03:39.216
Yes. Last week, my post went viral!

69
00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:43.015
Wow! Did you check your privacy settings?

70
00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:46.061
Not yet. Should I?

71
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.545
Yes, you should. And you must protect your digital footprint.

72
00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:55.777
Good advice. I shouldn't share my address or my school name.

73
00:03:56.933 --> 00:03:58.260
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:01.708
Grammar focus: Modal verbs of advice.

75
00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.242
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.077
You should check privacy settings.

77
00:04:06.983 --> 00:04:09.169
You must protect your digital footprint.

78
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.897
You shouldn't share your password.

79
00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:17.436
'Must' is stronger than 'should'. Use 'must' for rules and very important advice.

80
00:04:18.183 --> 00:04:22.473
Be careful! Don't say: You should to check your privacy settings.

81
00:04:24.433 --> 00:04:27.234
Say: You should check your privacy settings.

82
00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.534
Don't use 'to' after 'should' or 'must'.

83
00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:32.916
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.084
My Viral Post.

85
00:04:35.384 --> 00:04:39.288
Last month, my post went viral because of a trending hashtag.

86
00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.194
Thousands of people liked it, and I got many new followers.

87
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.815
Some comments were kind, but some were rude.

88
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.622
Now I always check my privacy settings to protect my digital footprint.

89
00:04:52.633 --> 00:04:56.421
You should think before you post, because the internet never forgets.

90
00:04:57.533 --> 00:05:01.674
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:02.517 --> 00:05:04.319
You blank share your password.

92
00:05:04.619 --> 00:05:08.110
A, mustn't. B, must. C, should.

93
00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.434
The answer is A: mustn't.

94
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:17.256
Shared very quickly by many people is blank.

95
00:05:17.556 --> 00:05:21.105
A, viral. B, private. C, digital.

96
00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.701
The answer is A: viral.

97
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.535
The computer rules that choose what you see are the blank.

98
00:05:30.835 --> 00:05:34.871
A, algorithm. B, hashtag. C, platform.

99
00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:40.712
The answer is A: algorithm.

100
00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.226
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:48.779
How do you use social media responsibly?

102
00:05:57.583 --> 00:05:59.002
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:59.302 --> 00:06:10.108
I use social media responsibly. I should only post kind things, and I must never share my password. I also check my privacy settings often.

104
00:06:10.408 --> 00:06:12.221
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:13.117 --> 00:06:17.859
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and modal verbs of advice.

106
00:06:18.159 --> 00:06:23.122
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

107
00:06:23.422 --> 00:06:26.178
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:26.478 --> 00:06:29.166
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

